    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nAdded email uniqueness enforcement as a new, self-contained pipeline step \u2014 mirroring the existing telephone-duplicate rule, so no existing function grew.\n\n**New files (each a small, cohesive unit with zero surrounding class complexity):**\n- `RejectDuplicateOwnerEmail.java` \u2014 one `service` method: skips absent/blank emails, else scans owners and throws `DuplicateOwnerEmailException` when a lower-cased email collides.\n- `DuplicateOwnerEmailException.java` \u2014 checked exception (so it appears in `throws`).\n- `DuplicateOwnerEmailExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT`.\n- `DuplicateOwnerEmailException.yml` escalation mapping.\n\n**One-line wiring change:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted `rejectDuplicateEmail` right after `normalizeEmail`, so the comparison uses the already-lower-cased value.\n\n**Structural-impact note:** I placed the logic after `NormalizeOwnerEmail` (which already lower-cases the request email) rather than editing that class, so no existing function's body or complexity changed. The one edited file (the YAML) touches only a low-complexity, declarative step list. All new behaviour lives in fresh classes with `WMC_other \u2248 0`.",
